drizzik@aol.com (Drizzik) writes:

>What exactly are "Bones" levels? Do your old characters actually come
>back as monsters? :)

When you die, there is a 1/3 chance that the level you die on will be
saved as a "bones" level. When this happens, the level is saved,
exactly as it was when you died (it contains the same monsters, the
same items, the same whatever).

Only three things of note change: YOU get changed into a ghost, most of
the stuff you were carrying gets cursed, and if you were carrying the
Amulet of Yendor, it becomes a cheap plastic imitation. There are
probably more changes to the level, but these are less important.

Note that the reason why you dies (usually a monster) ALSO remains on
the level, making it potentially dangerous.

